@startuml
' Pedagogical backend-pattern diagram for the background chapter, drawn in the
' same class-diagram style as the Chapter 4 figures: a stable user-facing class
' holds in one slot an interchangeable backend object that decides where the
' data actually live.
'
' Checked against the sources:
'   Spectra/R/Spectra.R:369-383             slot backend = "MsBackend"
'   Chromatograms/R/Chromatograms.R:280-287 slot backend = "ChromBackend"
'   Spectra/R/MsBackend.R:937-943           MsBackend contains "VIRTUAL"
'   Chromatograms/R/ChromBackend.R:529-535  ChromBackend contains "VIRTUAL"
' The three backend boxes are storage roles, not class names: each stands for a
' concrete subclass of the virtual backend class (stated in the figure caption).
' Smetana layout: renders without a Graphviz/dot installation.
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadow false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 26
skinparam ranksep 36
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor #777777
  ArrowColor #555555
}
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #fafafa
  BorderColor #aaaaaa
}
hide empty members
hide <<written once>> circle
hide <<role>> circle
hide <<role>> stereotype

class "Analysis code" as A <<written once>>
class "Spectra / Chromatograms" as I <<S4 class>> {
  backend
  --
  intensity()
  mz()
  filter*()
}
abstract class "MsBackend / ChromBackend" as B <<virtual>>

together {
  class "in memory" as M <<role>>
  class "on disk\n(mzML via mzR)" as D <<role>>
  class "remote archive\n(downloaded on demand)" as R <<role>>
}

A ..> I : calls intensity(x), mz(x), ...
I *-- "1" B : backend slot
B <|-- M
B <|-- D
B <|-- R

@enduml
